    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--1\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p><strong>石像鬼Gargoyle</strong></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\">這些土元素構成的怪異生物，長着惡魔般的外觀且充滿惡意，它們正是立在大樓樓頂上那些非活體石像鬼塑像的原型。石像鬼潛伏在磚石與廢墟之間，它們像普通石像一樣一動不動，然後等待着享受自己打破靜止那一剎那的給人帶來的恐怖，以及施予他人痛苦時的愉悅。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>活化之石Animate Stone。</strong></em>石像鬼偏好待在巖地邊緣與山崖，或是地底洞窟的巖架上。它們在城市房頂上出沒，禿鷹一般盤旋於石拱門或城堡教堂一類建築的牆垛上。它們還會一動不動的表現如一尊非活體的石像，也正因此而時常被用作哨兵。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>惡名遠揚Deadly Reputation。</strong></em>石像鬼以殘忍聞名於世。來自無數種文化的各式建築上都會雕刻有仿照石像鬼的雕像，正是用其形象以嚇退某些不速之客。儘管這些塑像只有裝飾作用，但真正的石像鬼卻時常躲藏其中對那些毫無防備的目標發動伏擊。守望時的石像鬼會捕捉鳥類和齧齒類來作消遣，但長時間的等候依然使其傷害智能生物的慾望不斷增長。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>殘暴僕從Cruel Servants。</strong></em>石像鬼非常容易受擁狡猾睿智的主人所鼓舞。它們偏愛一些簡單的任務，諸如爲主人護家，折磨殘殺闖門者，以及任何其他花最小的力氣又能最大限度製造痛苦和屠殺的勾當。<br />石像鬼由於其趨向混亂和破壞的惡意習性而時常爲一些惡魔工作。強大的施法者還可以輕易的將石像鬼招募爲護衛爲其看家護院。石像鬼有着頑石一樣的堅韌與耐性，甚至可以長年爲最殘忍的主人服務而不帶一點怨言。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>元素本質Elemental Nature。</strong></em>石像鬼無需空氣、飲食和睡眠。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"></p><p class=\"p\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:5pt 0pt 5pt 21pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan;mso-para-margin-left:2.0000gd;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto\"><strong>邪惡元素碎片Shards of Elemental Evil</strong></p><p class=\"16\" style=\"MARGIN:0pt 0pt 0pt 21pt;LINE-HEIGHT:13pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan;mso-para-margin-left:2.0000gd;mso-line-height-rule:exactly\">邪惡土元素親王Prince of Elemental Earth，歐雷莫克Ogremoch行走在它的石之領域時，會在其身後留下破碎的岩石碎片。這些滿溢知覺的殘片迸發着元素主君的精華，經年累月的成長爲近似類人生物的岩石形態，並最終形成冷酷兇殘的石像鬼之形。<br />歐雷莫克並非有意的創造出石像鬼，而這些生物確實是其自身邪惡本質的物質化表現。石像鬼是沉重卻懂得飛行的活體岩石。其存在正好讓歐雷莫克用來嘲諷那些被自己鄙視的氣之元素。這些生物如同其造物主一樣從本源上厭惡氣元素族類（尤其是阿蘭寇拉鷹人aarakocra），且隨時隨地都想將它們消滅殆盡。<br />石像鬼在其家園位面中揚起土灰，讓歐雷莫克得以闖入氣元素位面的阿卡Aaqa，也即是棲息着阿蘭寇拉鷹人，和那些受鷹人們侍奉，慈悲的氣之公爵們所在的領地。</p><p>The inanimate gargoyles that perch atop great buildings are inspired by these malevolent creatures of elemental earth that resemble grotesque, fiendish statues. A gargoyle lurks among masonry and ruins, as still as any stone sculpture, and delights in the terror it creates when it breaks from its suspended pose, as well as the pain it inflicts on its victims.</p><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Animate Stone\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Animate Stone.</span> Gargoyles cling to rocky cliffs and mountains, or roost on ledges in underground caves. They haunt city rooftops, perching vulture-like among the high stone arches and buttresses of castles and cathedrals, and they can hold themselves so still that they appear inanimate. Able to maintain this state for years, a gargoyle makes an ideal sentry.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Deadly Reputation\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Deadly Reputation.</span> Gargoyles have a reputation for cruelty. Statues carved into the likenesses of gargoyles appear in the architecture of countless cultures to frighten away trespassers. Although such sculptures are only decorative, real gargoyles can hide among them to ambush unsuspecting victims. A gargoyle might alleviate the tedium of its watch by catching and tormenting birds or rodents, but its long wait only increases its craving for harming sentient creatures.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Cruel Servants\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Cruel Servants.</span> Gargoyles are easily inspired by the cunning of an intelligent master. They enjoy simple tasks such as guarding a master's home, torturing and killing interlopers, and anything else that involves minimum effort and maximum pain and carnage.</p><p>Gargoyles sometimes serve demons for their propensity for wanton chaos and destruction. Powerful spellcasters can also easily enlist gargoyle guardians to keep watch over their gates and walls. Gargoyles have the patience and fortitude of stone, and will serve even the cruelest master for years without complaint.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Elemental Nature\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Elemental Nature.</span> A gargoyle doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.</p></div><div class=\"rd__b-special rd__b-inset\" data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Shards of Elemental Evil\"><h4 class=\"rd__h rd__h--2-inset\" data-title-index=\"5\"><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Shards of Elemental Evil</span></h4><p>As Ogrémoch, the evil Prince of Elemental Earth, treads his stony realm, it leaves shards of broken rock in his wake. Imbued with slivers of sentience, these shards thrum with the essence of the elemental prince, growing over long years into vaguely humanoid rock formations that resolve at last into the hard, cruel shapes of gargoyles.</p><p>Ogrémoch doesn't create gargoyles deliberately, but they are a physical manifestation of his evil. Gargoyles are mockeries of the elemental air that Ogrémoch despises. They are heavy creatures of living stone, yet capable of flight. Like their creator, they possess a fundamental hatred for beings of elemental air, aarakocra in particular, and relish every opportunity to destroy such creatures.</p><p>On their home plane, gargoyles carve out earth motes that Ogrémoch hurtles into Aaqa, the domain of the aarakocra and the benevolent Wind Dukes the bird folk serve in the Elemental Plane of Air.</p></div></div></div>",
